WEBVTT

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:05.480
The man who turned

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:09.350
Tsukikage, Crow, and the five 
Academia students into cards

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:12.320
was a man truly worthy of the 
name, "Battle Beast."

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.840
He easily dominated Gongenzaka and me.

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.060
But nevertheless, Gongenzaka had faith in me.

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:25.370
Action Spell Benkei Guard!

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:28.640
I Special Summon one Benkei 
Token in attack position!

00:00:29.040 --> 00:00:32.380
You cannot attack anything 
but this Benkei Token,

00:00:32.380 --> 00:00:34.920
and this token cannot be destroyed by battle!

00:00:39.130 --> 00:00:40.220
Gongenzaka!

00:00:41.410 --> 00:00:42.810
Gongenzaka...

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:45.190
picked up an Action Card?

00:00:45.480 --> 00:00:46.840
Gongenzaka...

00:00:46.840 --> 00:00:50.430
By doing that, you can't use your deck!

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:52.600
From now on,

00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:55.360
I, the man Gongenzaka, shall face you.

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:57.640
You will not lay one hand on Yuya!

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.480
Gongenzaka!

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:24.950
Go, Yuya.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.900
Even alone, you... You should...

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.240
Hold on.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:36.070
I'll turn you into a card now.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.040
Gongenzaka!

00:01:56.800 --> 00:01:59.760
In a world split into four dimensions,

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:03.440
four boys exist, all with the same face.

00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:07.180
Their dragons call to each other,

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:10.570
almost as if seeking one another.

00:03:44.170 --> 00:03:49.010
The Stigma of Misfortune

00:03:49.870 --> 00:03:50.800
Is that...

00:03:50.800 --> 00:03:52.010
I-It can't be.

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:53.650
No, it is him!

00:03:53.650 --> 00:03:55.450
Jack Atlas!

00:03:55.450 --> 00:03:57.080
Sorry I'm late, Yuya!

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:05.860
2000-point penalty for entering the battle.

00:04:08.150 --> 00:04:11.850
Late? Is he another of the Lancers?

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.580
I do not join any faction.

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:17.910
But I will not deny that I am an ally...

00:04:19.250 --> 00:04:23.310
Of the entertainment duelist I have 
acknowledged, Yuya Sakaki!

00:04:23.310 --> 00:04:24.580
Jack...

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:28.510
Leave this to Yuya and me, and stand back.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.090
R-Right.

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:34.640
Were you able to hang on like that 
because you knew Jack was coming?

00:04:34.640 --> 00:04:36.980
No way... I couldn't have known.

00:04:36.980 --> 00:04:40.200
But no matter how badly 
he beat us, I believed

00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.260
that as long as I protected Yuya, 
a miracle would occur.

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:46.240
Thank you, Jack.

00:04:46.240 --> 00:04:49.860
I thought we'd meet again 
someday, but not like this...

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:53.770
I felt I had a responsibility to see 
where City would go next.

00:04:54.130 --> 00:04:59.110
A responsibility to see both 
Tops and Commons gone,

00:04:59.110 --> 00:05:01.300
and a new age come to City.

00:05:01.700 --> 00:05:02.500
But...

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:05.950
Crow and the others already left.

00:05:05.950 --> 00:05:08.640
Leave City's future to us!

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:13.050
Jack, work with them to fight Academia!

00:05:13.050 --> 00:05:14.690
To save the world!

00:05:15.090 --> 00:05:16.540
The kids said that?

00:05:16.540 --> 00:05:17.360
Yes.

00:05:17.900 --> 00:05:22.340
I crossed dimensions at the urging of 
those children who adore Crow.

00:05:24.130 --> 00:05:25.180
Crow...

00:05:25.840 --> 00:05:27.950
So, where is he now?

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.310
He's...

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:33.110
Crow...

00:05:33.640 --> 00:05:35.480
Trying to protect me...

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:37.270
I'm sorry.

00:05:37.270 --> 00:05:39.450
If we'd been more capable...

00:05:39.450 --> 00:05:41.920
The one who defeated Crow...

00:05:41.920 --> 00:05:43.420
Was it you?!

00:05:44.500 --> 00:05:46.160
And if it was?

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.590
I'll make you pay.

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:52.130
For the sake of the children who 
saw me off, I will crush you!

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:53.580
Interesting.

00:05:53.580 --> 00:05:58.430
To talk that big, he must be quite confident.

00:05:58.430 --> 00:06:00.870
Show me, then...

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:04.430
Show me how you stand against 
the strongest Battle Beast

00:06:04.430 --> 00:06:06.780
that I raised at Academia.

00:06:06.780 --> 00:06:10.390
I set one card and end my turn.

00:06:11.180 --> 00:06:16.020
Even if he's the strongest at Academia, 
Jack is City's best duelist.

00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.890
In a tag team with Yuya, 
the man he acknowledges,

00:06:18.890 --> 00:06:20.880
there's no way they can lose.

00:06:20.880 --> 00:06:23.960
Yeah, we're counting on you, Jack Atlas!

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:26.650
If you wish to see, I shall show you...

00:06:26.930 --> 00:06:31.780
The form of duel that I refined in what 
you call the "Synchro Dimension"!

00:06:32.140 --> 00:06:34.340
My turn!

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:36.570
First, I set one card!

00:06:37.810 --> 00:06:39.560
A set card, right off the bat?

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.280
I summon Tuner Monster Red 
Resonator from my hand!

00:06:49.250 --> 00:06:52.670
When I summon a Red monster to the field,

00:06:52.670 --> 00:06:57.230
I can Special Summon Red Warg from 
my hand, with attack points halved.

00:07:02.670 --> 00:07:07.940
Level 2 Red Resonator tunes 
Level 6 Red Warg!

00:07:08.640 --> 00:07:11.980
The cry of the champion shakes 
heaven and earth.

00:07:11.980 --> 00:07:15.550
Let the conqueror's unique power 
be carved into your body!

00:07:15.550 --> 00:07:17.190
Synchro Summon.

00:07:18.080 --> 00:07:20.810
The raging soul...

00:07:20.810 --> 00:07:23.290
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:07:31.540 --> 00:07:32.630
Let's go!

00:07:35.770 --> 00:07:39.240
Once per turn, Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:44.140
can destroy all Special Summoned monsters 
with equal or fewer attack points.

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:47.370
And for each, it deals you 
500 points of damage.

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:50.480
Absolute Power Flame!

00:07:51.910 --> 00:07:54.200
That dragon has 3000 attack points?

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:58.360
So, he destroys all Special Summoned 
monsters with fewer points?

00:07:58.360 --> 00:08:03.060
The Synchro Dimension has monsters 
with such amazing effects?

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:06.040
That effect is nothing!

00:08:06.040 --> 00:08:12.040
I activate Continuous Trap, Gladiator Beast's 
Medusa Shield, targeting Gyzarus!

00:08:14.770 --> 00:08:17.610
I negate the destruction of Gyzarus.

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:21.090
Counter Trap Red Vanish!

00:08:21.090 --> 00:08:24.430
When a Red monster is on 
my side of the field,

00:08:24.430 --> 00:08:27.190
I can activate this card on 
the turn that it was set.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.040
What?

00:08:28.040 --> 00:08:31.290
A trap he can activate on the turn it was set?

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:35.990
I negate a spell or trap card activated 
by you, and destroy it!

00:08:40.930 --> 00:08:44.160
Wow! 1500 damage at once!

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:45.240
Huh?

00:08:45.240 --> 00:08:47.860
It was 500 damage, wasn't it?

00:08:47.860 --> 00:08:51.720
It's the effect of his Continuous 
Trap Thumbs Down.

00:08:51.720 --> 00:08:53.040
Of course!

00:08:53.040 --> 00:08:55.690
The trap that deals 500 points of damage

00:08:55.690 --> 00:08:58.540
to the one who controls destroyed cards!

00:08:58.540 --> 00:09:02.330
By destroying Medusa Shield and Gyzarus,

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:06.360
1000 points were added to Absolute 
Power Flame's damage.

00:09:06.980 --> 00:09:08.330
Damn you...

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:11.830
You set that Counter Trap, anticipating this?

00:09:11.830 --> 00:09:14.410
I merely thought that a duelist

00:09:14.410 --> 00:09:19.680
who gave Yuya Sakaki this much of a 
fight must have something to him.

00:09:19.680 --> 00:09:20.770
Jack...

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:24.270
Too bad!

00:09:24.270 --> 00:09:30.080
Cheap tricks won't work before my soul, 
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:09:30.920 --> 00:09:34.920
To overturn my trap...

00:09:34.920 --> 00:09:38.040
BB's life is down to 1100.

00:09:38.040 --> 00:09:40.890
The enemy monster has 3000 attack points!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:43.600
If he takes a direct attack from that...

00:09:49.130 --> 00:09:54.280
Unfortunately, on the same turn I use 
Red Warg's effect, I cannot attack.

00:09:55.320 --> 00:09:57.010
A stay of execution.

00:10:00.210 --> 00:10:02.680
What are you smiling about?

00:10:02.680 --> 00:10:04.380
Don't be ridiculous!

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.600
You are my masterpiece.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:10.560
Academia's strongest duelist!

00:10:10.840 --> 00:10:13.520
I've never created a better duelist.

00:10:13.520 --> 00:10:19.030
And you are relieved when this man says 
he'll give you a stay of execution?

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:23.680
In that case, I'll have to personally direct you!

00:10:23.680 --> 00:10:26.160
2000-point penalty for entering the battle.

00:10:26.160 --> 00:10:26.970
The instructor?

00:10:26.970 --> 00:10:29.710
Instructor Sanders is participating himself?

00:10:29.710 --> 00:10:31.120
The instructor, eh?

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:32.240
Interesting.

00:10:32.240 --> 00:10:34.220
Instruct us, then!

00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:37.540
I set two cards and end my turn!

00:10:39.250 --> 00:10:43.860
In that instant, the effect of the Medusa 
Shield in my graveyard activates.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:49.130
I choose one Gladiator Beast 
trap in my deck...

00:10:50.690 --> 00:10:51.980
And set it!

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:56.550
My turn!

00:10:58.080 --> 00:11:02.710
I activate my spell card Test 
Fusion from my hand!

00:11:02.960 --> 00:11:08.110
Its effect lets me send Test Ape and Test 
Tiger from my hand to my graveyard,

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:12.270
to Fusion Summon, ignoring the 
fusion requirements!

00:11:12.270 --> 00:11:15.770
Enslaved ape-man, come together 
with the tiger that shares your fate,

00:11:15.770 --> 00:11:18.320
and invite your whip-cracking master!

00:11:18.320 --> 00:11:20.290
Fusion Summon!

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:25.600
Appear, Gladiator Beast Tamer Editor!

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:30.740
I activate Editor's effect.

00:11:30.740 --> 00:11:35.610
Once per turn, I can choose one Gladiator 
Beast from an Extra Deck and,

00:11:35.610 --> 00:11:38.010
ignoring its summon requirements,

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:41.250
Special Summon it to its controller's field.

00:11:41.250 --> 00:11:47.960
I choose Gladiator Beast Andabata 
in BB's Extra Deck!

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:51.340
That troublesome monster is back?

00:11:51.340 --> 00:11:53.660
And he summoned it from BB's deck?

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:58.000
Does that mean he can freely summon 
other people's monsters?

00:11:58.000 --> 00:11:59.260
Of course.

00:11:59.260 --> 00:12:02.130
Editor controls the Gladiator Beasts.

00:12:02.130 --> 00:12:06.100
He can bring them to heel with a crack 
of his whip, no matter how fierce.

00:12:06.470 --> 00:12:08.110
Now, BB...

00:12:08.110 --> 00:12:11.080
I've returned the monster to 
your side of the field.

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:13.630
You can fight to your heart's content.

00:12:13.630 --> 00:12:19.250
Show your strength and your ferocity 
to the enemy before you!

00:12:22.150 --> 00:12:23.100
He's...

00:12:23.100 --> 00:12:23.900
What's wrong?

00:12:24.520 --> 00:12:27.690
It just seemed like he was 
acting a little differently...

00:12:27.690 --> 00:12:28.600
Go!

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:32.120
This is a direct order from the Professor.

00:12:32.120 --> 00:12:35.850
All Lancers, except Reiji Akaba, are to be purged.

00:12:35.850 --> 00:12:36.930
In particular,

00:12:36.930 --> 00:12:42.260
you must not let the man named 
Yuya Sakaki escape.

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:44.030
Yuya?

00:12:44.030 --> 00:12:45.310
Specifically him?

00:12:45.760 --> 00:12:49.610
Wh-Why does the head of Academia...

00:12:51.160 --> 00:12:52.410
Revival Zero...

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:57.640
Surely, this is at the heart 
of Leo Akaba's plan.

00:12:57.640 --> 00:13:00.190
And given the existence of Joeri...

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:03.530
Yuya, you must be connected, too.

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:04.660
I'm...

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:08.620
I'm involved in Academia's plan?

00:13:12.210 --> 00:13:15.770
Why did the Professor 
name me, personally?

00:13:16.140 --> 00:13:19.080
Whatever your leader's order,

00:13:19.080 --> 00:13:23.250
I will not let Academia accomplish it, 
not as long as I am with Yuya!

00:13:23.250 --> 00:13:25.690
Bragging again?

00:13:25.690 --> 00:13:29.050
An eyesore like you can begone at once!

00:13:29.050 --> 00:13:32.990
When there are two or more 
Gladiator Beasts on the field,

00:13:32.990 --> 00:13:35.870
Editor's effect can destroy one monster,

00:13:35.870 --> 00:13:40.260
dealing its attack points as damage 
to the player who controls it.

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:45.800
I destroy the 3000-attack-point 
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend!

00:13:46.140 --> 00:13:48.860
That dragon's controller has 2000 life points!

00:13:48.860 --> 00:13:50.720
Which means if the effect goes through...

00:13:50.720 --> 00:13:55.910
That's right! You're finished, Jack Atlas!

00:13:55.910 --> 00:13:58.700
I activate my trap Red Armor!

00:13:59.160 --> 00:14:02.700
This turn, Red monsters cannot 
be destroyed by effects!

00:14:03.940 --> 00:14:08.910
Then, grind your teeth as you watch Yuya 
Sakaki's defeat before your very eyes!

00:14:08.910 --> 00:14:12.870
Editor attacks Yuya Sakaki directly!

00:14:18.690 --> 00:14:19.930
What are you doing?

00:14:19.930 --> 00:14:20.800
Yuya!

00:14:26.940 --> 00:14:28.190
It's no use...

00:14:28.190 --> 00:14:31.120
You can't escape Editor's attack!

00:14:33.670 --> 00:14:35.020
Don't let him get it, BB!

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:39.120
Damn you... Why didn't you move?

00:14:40.030 --> 00:14:42.030
Action Spell Evasion!

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.730
I negate the effect of one of your monsters!

00:14:45.660 --> 00:14:47.500
Yes! He dodged it!

00:14:48.160 --> 00:14:51.470
Damn you! Why won't you obey my orders?

00:14:51.940 --> 00:14:55.670
This is why you could never 
become a proper soldier!

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:58.650
On a battlefield, your superior's 
orders are absolute.

00:14:58.650 --> 00:15:02.830
Ignoring them to do what you like 
won't only let victory escape,

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:04.920
but will put your allies in danger.

00:15:04.920 --> 00:15:07.210
Everyone, engrave this on your hearts.

00:15:07.210 --> 00:15:10.390
Your commanding officer's orders 
are absolute and ironclad!

00:15:10.390 --> 00:15:11.450
Do you get that?

00:15:11.450 --> 00:15:12.360
Yes, sir!

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:16.930
Nice words from a guy whose orders 
got five students turned to cards.

00:15:16.930 --> 00:15:19.360
I end my turn.

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.440
Okay... Go, Yuya!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.280
Crush that creepy guy and—

00:15:24.280 --> 00:15:25.340
Yuya?

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:29.270
What are you thinking about?

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:31.210
Leo Akaba.

00:15:31.680 --> 00:15:34.480
What does he know about us?

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:35.740
Us?

00:15:35.740 --> 00:15:41.610
Reiji said that Joeri and I might 
be part of Academia's plan.

00:15:42.050 --> 00:15:46.780
Which means you and Hugo, who have 
the same face, might be, as well.

00:15:47.480 --> 00:15:50.520
We were all born in different dimensions.

00:15:51.520 --> 00:15:55.670
But we've met, again and again, 
as if guided by fate.

00:15:56.070 --> 00:15:59.430
And you and I now share a body...

00:16:02.470 --> 00:16:05.760
I've been wondering for so 
long how that happened,

00:16:05.760 --> 00:16:07.600
and I still have no answer.

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.170
But it's possible that Leo Akaba...

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:15.220
You think he knows the reason 
I merged with you?

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:16.510
Yeah.

00:16:16.510 --> 00:16:20.950
The reason he named me for 
elimination might also be...

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:23.530
No, it's definitely connected!

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:27.630
After all, ever since we joined together,

00:16:28.080 --> 00:16:31.100
those terrible things have happened.

00:16:31.670 --> 00:16:35.570
I forgot myself in anger, and the next 
thing I knew, my opponent...

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:39.040
The time our four dragons were in one place...

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:45.930
Back then, we heard a voice 
from the bottom of our hearts.

00:16:45.930 --> 00:16:48.850
Yeah, it didn't come from you or me.

00:16:49.150 --> 00:16:54.330
There's something, I don't know what, 
buried deep in our hearts.

00:16:54.700 --> 00:16:58.300
Are you saying Leo Akaba knows what it is?

00:16:58.300 --> 00:17:01.660
Yeah... That's why he singled me out!

00:17:01.660 --> 00:17:04.000
Wake up, Yuya!

00:17:04.600 --> 00:17:09.210
In the middle of a duel, to avert one's 
eyes from battle is unforgivable!

00:17:09.860 --> 00:17:11.530
Why do you hesitate?

00:17:11.530 --> 00:17:15.450
If there is hesitation in your heart, 
communicate it with your duel!

00:17:15.450 --> 00:17:17.150
Shout it with the duel!

00:17:17.150 --> 00:17:20.270
There's no reason to hesitate! 
Get him, Yuya!

00:17:20.270 --> 00:17:23.080
Avenge Crow and Tsukikage!

00:17:23.080 --> 00:17:25.090
Don't let your comrade's sacrifice be in vain!

00:17:25.660 --> 00:17:27.790
Crow... Tsukikage...

00:17:28.520 --> 00:17:29.730
That's right.

00:17:29.730 --> 00:17:33.460
To allow us to move forward, they both...

00:17:34.060 --> 00:17:38.540
If I don't want those feelings to have 
been in vain, I must win this duel!

00:17:39.000 --> 00:17:40.370
My turn!

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:44.340
I summon Performapal 
Pararhino from my hand!

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:53.180
Once per turn, Pararhino can negate 
one of your monster's effects.

00:17:53.180 --> 00:17:56.140
I choose Andabata!

00:17:56.520 --> 00:18:00.650
All right! Now, even if he returns 
Andabata to his Extra Deck this turn,

00:18:00.650 --> 00:18:03.630
he can't Special Summon another monster!

00:18:03.950 --> 00:18:06.020
And Pararhino's effect

00:18:06.020 --> 00:18:09.330
lets me Special Summon Performapal 
Gongato from my hand!

00:18:12.800 --> 00:18:17.850
And Gongato sets Andabata's 
attack points equal to its own.

00:18:19.680 --> 00:18:20.470
Battle!

00:18:20.470 --> 00:18:23.950
Pararhino attacks Andabata!

00:18:26.120 --> 00:18:30.090
The effect of Continuous Trap 
Gladiator Beast's Medallion

00:18:30.090 --> 00:18:32.060
prevents Andabata's destruction!

00:18:32.060 --> 00:18:35.760
But its effect means that the 
damage you take is doubled!

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:43.930
I activate my Continuous Trap 
Gladiator Beast's Assault Fort!

00:18:45.720 --> 00:18:49.210
When I take damage from battle 
with a Gladiator Beast,

00:18:49.210 --> 00:18:53.650
I destroy a non-Gladiator Beast 
card on my side of the field!

00:18:53.650 --> 00:18:59.420
Then, I negate one Gladiator 
Beast spell or trap card,

00:18:59.420 --> 00:19:03.190
to treat it as a Continuous Spell 
Gladiator Beast's Assault Fort.

00:19:07.470 --> 00:19:12.400
I treat Gladiator Beast's Virtue and 
Gladiator Beast's Medallion

00:19:12.720 --> 00:19:14.600
as Gladiator Beast's Assault Forts!

00:19:21.710 --> 00:19:27.310
Once per each of our turns, when a 
Gladiator Beast does battle,

00:19:27.310 --> 00:19:31.280
Gladiator Beast's Assault Fort negates its 
destruction, reducing damage to 0.

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.620
And destruction by card effects is negated.

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:35.710
What?

00:19:35.710 --> 00:19:38.320
Then they can't do anything against you!

00:19:38.320 --> 00:19:42.250
And the effect of Gladiator Beast's Assault Fort

00:19:42.250 --> 00:19:47.500
lets me set one Gladiator Beast in each fort.

00:19:47.500 --> 00:19:51.700
In the first fort, I set Gladiator Beast Augustus.

00:19:51.700 --> 00:19:55.040
In the second fort, I set Gladiator Beast Laquari.

00:19:55.360 --> 00:19:58.990
And when the monster in either fort 
is returned to my deck,

00:19:58.990 --> 00:20:03.280
I deal another 1000 points of 
damage to my opponent!

00:20:03.280 --> 00:20:04.700
1000 damage?

00:20:04.700 --> 00:20:06.020
Are you kidding me?

00:20:07.190 --> 00:20:08.520
What do you think?

00:20:08.520 --> 00:20:10.370
This is my trump card!

00:20:10.370 --> 00:20:13.640
Break through it, if you think you can!

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:25.690
He's actually...

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:29.640
I end my turn.

00:20:31.200 --> 00:20:32.880
Ending your turn, eh?

00:20:33.510 --> 00:20:35.400
Now, it's your turn...

00:20:35.400 --> 00:20:38.850
Bury both Jack Atlas and Yuya Sakaki!

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:41.320
What?

00:20:44.440 --> 00:20:46.760
What are you doing? This is an order!

00:20:46.760 --> 00:20:50.640
An order from me... no, from the Professor!

00:20:50.640 --> 00:20:52.360
I won't allow you to ignore it!

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:55.430
Why won't you fight?

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:58.040
Abandoning a fight is equivalent to losing.

00:20:58.040 --> 00:21:00.440
Do you want to be turned into a card?!

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:06.190
Do it, BB!

00:21:06.190 --> 00:21:09.570
If you don't want to be turned into a card,

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:11.610
you must destroy every one of them!

00:21:12.180 --> 00:21:14.050
My turn!

00:21:16.150 --> 00:21:19.900
When two or more Gladiator 
Beasts are on the field,

00:21:19.900 --> 00:21:24.360
a Gladiator Beast's controller 
can activate Editor's effect.

00:21:24.360 --> 00:21:26.680
Yes... Good, BB...

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:32.370
If you use its effect to destroy Jack Atlas's 
Scarlight Red Dragon Archfiend,

00:21:32.370 --> 00:21:34.610
you'll deal 3000 damage.

00:21:34.610 --> 00:21:36.380
I destroy

00:21:36.840 --> 00:21:40.380
Gladiator Beast Tamer Editor itself!

00:21:40.380 --> 00:21:41.310
What?

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:48.580
And I deal its attack points, 2400, to you!

00:21:49.270 --> 00:21:52.460
Have you gone mad, BB?!

00:23:49.740 --> 00:23:53.480
You are the greatest and most 
terrible beast that I raised.

00:23:53.480 --> 00:23:56.680
Turn me into a card. Then erase Yuya Sakaki!

00:23:56.680 --> 00:23:58.480
More orders?

00:23:58.480 --> 00:24:02.050
If you let Yuya Sakaki escape, there will 
be no path to survival for you.

00:24:02.400 --> 00:24:03.660
Let your battle souls burn!

00:24:03.660 --> 00:24:07.890
Survive! Devour the strong, and 
make them your flesh and blood!

00:24:08.150 --> 00:24:10.940
Win and stand taller than anyone!

00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:15.820
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh! ARC-V: 
Glory on the Academia!

00:24:15.820 --> 00:24:17.940
The fun is only getting started!
